import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/pages.css';
---
<Base title="Privacy & local brief handling" description="How this website handles your locally prepared project brief, downloads, clipboard actions, and external links.">
  <section class="shell page-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Reachly Studio / Privacy</p><h1 class="display page-title">Your brief.<br /><em>Under your control.</em></h1><div class="intro-tail"><span class="signal-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><p class="lede">This notice explains the website as it works today. The project-brief tool prepares text in your browser; it is not a delivery or submission service.</p></div></section>
  <section class="shell privacy-layout section-space"><nav aria-label="On this page"><p class="eyebrow">In this notice</p><a href="#brief-data">Project brief</a><a href="#your-copy">Downloads & clipboard</a><a href="#site-data">Website data</a><a href="#external-links">External websites</a><a href="#future-contact">Contact & future changes</a></nav><div class="reading">
    <section id="brief-data"><h2 class="display">01 / Prepared locally.</h2><p>The brief tool asks for your name, business or project name, a reply address or phone number, the change you need, and an optional service interest. These details are used in the browser to validate your entries and create a readable project brief.</p><p>Your brief is <strong>not sent to Reachly</strong>, a form service, or a third-party API. There is no confirmed receiver connected to this tool. Do not include passwords, financial account details, identity documents, or other sensitive information.</p><p>The tool does not write your entries to localStorage, sessionStorage, or cookies. There is no application-level draft persistence. Refreshing or leaving the page can lose the draft; your browser may independently remember or restore form fields according to your browser settings. “Clear brief” removes entries and the generated review from the current page.</p></section>
    <section id="your-copy"><h2 class="display">02 / Copies you choose.</h2><p>Downloading creates a plain-text file on your device. Copying places the brief on your clipboard only when you choose the copy action. If clipboard access is unavailable, you can select the review text and copy it manually.</p><p>Your downloaded file, clipboard, browser history, shared device, and any later sharing are under your control. The website cannot remove a file after download or clear clipboard history maintained by your device. Share the text only through a channel you have independently verified.</p></section>
    <section id="site-data"><h2 class="display">03 / A small data footprint.</h2><p>This build contains no analytics, advertising pixels, or session-replay scripts. Names, reply details, messages, and exported brief contents are not placed in page URLs or analytics events by the application.</p><p>A link may include a public service slug, such as <code>?interest=seo</code>. Only an approved service value can preselect the brief interest. Other query fields do not fill your personal details. Avoid manually adding personal information to any URL.</p><p>Serving a website still involves normal network requests. A hosting provider may process request information such as an IP address, browser details, and requested URL according to its own configuration. This site notice does not claim that hosting infrastructure keeps no logs.</p></section>
    <section id="external-links"><h2 class="display">04 / Beyond this website.</h2><p>Project links take you to independent websites. Their content and data handling are controlled by those websites, not this local brief tool. Review their notices before supplying personal information. External project links open in a new tab.</p></section>
    <section id="future-contact"><h2 class="display">05 / Before delivery is enabled.</h2><p>A verified contact destination is not currently published or connected here. The brief tool cannot request a reply, make a booking, or establish an engagement. If you already know a verified contact channel, you can share your prepared brief there.</p><p>Before a delivery integration is enabled, this notice and the contact flow will need to explain the actual receiver, purpose, providers, retention, and available privacy contact. No legal entity, jurisdiction, or registration status is asserted by this notice.</p><a class="text-link" href="/contact">Return to the local brief tool <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  </div></section>
</Base>
